---
2026-09-07 (PDP audit): Found and fixed three instances of the same bug
class, all from the initial rebuild commit (a31cb76) — a hardcoded product
handle that never matched data/product.json's real Shopify handle
("acupressure-pen-meridian-massage-tool"):
  1. content/product-pen.ts `pen.handle` — was "acunova-acupressure-pen".
     This silenced isFlagship, which gated PenStory/PenMoments/PenVersus —
     the entire narrative section of the PDP (hardware stats, "two thousand
     years" story, comparison table) never rendered on the live product.
  2. data/reviews.ts `PEN_REVIEWS_HANDLE` — same wrong string. Silenced
     reviewSetForHandle(), so the PDP showed the empty "reviews are being
     collected" state despite real review content existing in the file.
  3. content/pitches.ts has an orphaned pitch for
     "acunova-replacement-head-set" — not a live bug (pitchFor() returns
     undefined safely), but there is no such SKU in the real catalog.
     Left as-is; flagged to user rather than deleted, in case a head-set
     listing is coming.
Generated the 4 missing /story/era-*.webp+avif images EraExplorer needs
(dormant until fix #1 landed, then live) and the 2 missing PWA icons
manifest.ts pointed at (0 icon files existed in public/ at all). Also fixed
manifest.ts theme_color/background_color, hardcoded to #ffffff instead of
the live teal palette.
Net effect: the real live PDP went from 5 sections with 2 broken images to
9 sections with 0 broken images, without any of the underlying component
code changing — it was 100% dead content becoming reachable via 3
one-line string fixes.

